  "notes": "Each boom length has 2-5 columns for different telescoping modes (sections I-V); the column marked ★ in the header was stored for every length (12 lengths). The document does NOT define ★ (UNVERIFIED meaning; it is typically the preferred/standard mode). Other modes sometimes give higher capacity at long radius (e.g. 21.1 m @10 m: 35.0 t vs ★ 33.5 t; 25.4 m @14 m: 20.5 vs ★ 19.0). 12.5 m @3.0-4.5 m values (80/78/76/70 t) are marked * : over sides and rear these require the 70 t, 80 t or 100 t hook (standard hook 60 t) and a special device above 70 t. 110 t @2.5 m is marked ** 'nominal' and excluded (null). Other tables: 19, 15, 11, 7, 3 t counterweight; standard counterweight 15 t, optional 8 t (total 23 t). The document does not state whether hook weight is included - assumed included, UNVERIFIED. Hooks: 60 t main (6 sheaves), 6.5 t aux, optional 80 t. Axle positions from carrier front per overall view chain (drawing rotated, front at bottom): (2095) boom overhang, 2785 front overhang, 1530 + 4270 + 1350 wheelbase, 2510 rear overhang, 460 = 15000 mm. Deadweight in driving condition 50 t (front axles 24 t, rear 26 t). Max lifting height main boom 59.2 m (excl. deflection). Transversal outrigger span 8.0 m fully / 5.3 m intermediate; longitudinal 6.38 m. Tyre size not given. Main boom: basic + 6 telescopic sections (single cylinder, pinned)."
